HST Office: HST Draw shows its ribbon again; an unused top-level image kept its notebookbar out of layout.

hst-ribbon-mockup-draw.patch moved the Arrange "Transform" button to imgHstArrangeTransformSmall and left
imgHstArrangeTransform defined at the top level of sdraw's notebookbar.ui with no button using it. VclBuilder
creates every top-level widget the .ui defines as a child window of the NotebookBar, and drops a GtkImage only
when a button takes it as its image. The leftover image stayed a second child of the NotebookBar, so
isLayoutEnabled() was false: the bar sized itself to that 24x30 image, the 21 tabs got a 6x3 pixel area and
Draw opened with no ribbon (and no menu bar, as the Tabbed mode hides it) on every platform since 1.0.2.
Removing the unused image gives the NotebookBar its single layout child again.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_ribbon_unused_images.py; runtime: HST Draw opens with its ribbon (fresh profile).
